<BaseLayout
  title="Splatoon 3 — Is the Digital Version Worth It?"
  description="Splatoon 3 buying guide: what's new, online requirements, and where to buy the digital key cheapest."
>
  <article class="post">
    <h1>Splatoon 3 — Is the Digital Version Worth It?</h1>
    <p class="meta">Nintendo Switch · Updated 2026-08-05</p>

    <p>
      <strong>Splatoon 3</strong> is Nintendo's colorful ink-splatting shooter, built
      around 4-v-4 turf wars and a surprising amount of single-player content. It's one
      of the best online multiplayer games on Switch.
    </p>

    <h2>What you get</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Turf War multiplayer</strong> — the core 4-v-4 mode, free to play online with Switch Online</li>
      <li><strong>Story mode (Return of the Mammalians)</strong> — a full solo campaign</li>
      <li><strong>Salmon Run</strong> — co-op wave survival, a fan favorite</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Digital vs physical</h2>
    <p>
      Splatoon 3 is a great digital pickup because you'll launch it constantly for quick
      online matches — no cartridge swapping. Digital keys through key stores like Green
      Man Gaming routinely beat the Nintendo eShop direct price, so it's worth comparing
      before you buy.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to buy cheapest</h2>
    <ul class="buy-list">
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="gmg"
          href="https://www.greenmangaming.com/search/?q=splatoon+3"
          cta="Check Green Man Gaming"
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="amazon"
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Splatoon+3+Switch"
          cta="Check on Amazon"
        />
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="note">
      Prices change frequently — always verify on the store before purchasing.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .post { padding: 1.5rem 0; max-width: 720px; }
  .post h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .buy-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
